  "prediction": "The report provides an analysis of various defense programs and issues for Congress, including helicopter programs, aircraft carriers, submarines, missile defense, bombers, armored vehicles, and infantry brigades. The report covers programs such as the VH-71/VXX Presidential Helicopter Program, Navy Ford Class Aircraft Carrier Program, Navy Virginia Class Attack Submarine Procurement, Navy Aegis Ballistic Missile Defense Program, Air Force KC-46A Tanker Aircraft Program, Navy Columbia Class Ballistic Missile Submarine Program, Conventional Prompt Global Strike and Long-Range Ballistic Missiles, Marine Corps Amphibious Combat Vehicle (ACV), Air Force Bomber Sustainment and Modernization, and Infantry Brigade Combat Team (IBCT) Mobility, Reconnaissance, and Firepower Programs. The report also includes insights on specific programs like the U.S. Army's Initial Maneuver, Short-Range Air Defense (IM-SHORAD) System and Air Force OA-X Light Attack Aircraft Program. The report is a valuable resource for Congress in understanding the background, current status, and issues related to these defense programs.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report provides an analysis of various defense programs and issues for Congress, including helicopter programs, aircraft carriers, submarines, missile defense, bombers, armored vehicles, and infantry brigades. The report covers programs such as the VH-71/VXX Presidential Helicopter Program, Navy Ford Class Aircraft Carrier Program, Navy Virginia Class Attack Submarine Procurement, Navy Aegis Ballistic Missile Defense Program, Air Force KC-46A Tanker Aircraft Program, Navy Columbia Class Ballistic Missile Submarine Program, Conventional Prompt Global Strike and Long-Range Ballistic Missiles, Marine Corps Amphibious Combat Vehicle (ACV), Air Force Bomber Sustainment and Modernization, and Infantry Brigade Combat Team (IBCT) Mobility, Reconnaissance, and Firepower Programs. The report also includes insights on specific programs like the U.S. Army's Initial Maneuver, Short-Range Air Defense (IM-SHORAD) System and Air Force OA-X Light Attack Aircraft Program. The report is a valuable resource for Congress in understanding the background, current status, and issues related to these defense programs.",
  "score": 14.33447052988388,
  "answers": [
    "The FY2019 Department of Defense Appropriations Act, enacted as Division A of P.L. 115-245 , provides $667.3 billion in new budget authority to fund all activities of the Department of Defense (DOD) except for the construction of military facilities and the operation of military family housing complexes. While the total amount appropriated for DOD for FY2019 was nearly equal to the Administration's request, the act provides more funding than requested for dozens of weapons acquisition programs, with the gross increase exceeding $10 billion. Those additions are offset by hundreds of reductions made elsewhere within the budget request. In effect, these reductions allowed Congress to add billions of dollars to the Administration's DOD budget request without exceeding the cap on defense spending that arose from the Bipartisan Budget Act of 2018 ( P.L. 115-123 ). That cap applies to discretionary appropriations for DOD's base budget \u2014that is, appropriations designated by Congress and the President as funding for emergencies or for Overseas Contingency Operations (OCO). OCO activities include current operations in Afghanistan and Syria, and any other operations which are so designated by Congress and the President. A House-Senate conference committee reported a version of the bill on September 13, 2018. The Senate approved the conference report on September 18 by a vote of 93-7 and the House did likewise on September 26 by a vote of 361-61. President Donald J. Trump signed the bill into law ( P.L. 115-245 ) on September 28, 2018. As enacted, H.R. 6157 funds the Administration's major defense initiatives, including an increase of 16,500 active-duty military personnel. Among the weapons procurement programs for which the bill provides substantial additions add to the amounts requested are the F-35 Joint Strike Fighter used by the Air Force, Navy, and Marine Corps (77 aircraft requested and 93 funded) and the Navy's Littoral Combat Ship (one requested and three funded)."
  ],
